{
  "step_1": "The decision reason is based on comparing the variances of the two lotteries and preferring the one with the larger variance. Variance can be computed from the outcomes and their probabilities. For Lottery A: outcomes are 4000 (25%), 2000 (25%), and 0 (50%). The expected value is (4000×0.25) + (2000×0.25) + (0×0.5) = 1000 + 500 + 0 = 1500. Variance = (4000−1500)²×0.25 + (2000−1500)²×0.25 + (0−1500)²×0.5 = (2500)²×0.25 + (500)²×0.25 + (1500)²×0.5 = 1,562,500 + 62,500 + 1,125,000 = 2,750,000. For Lottery B: outcomes are 6000 (25%) and 0 (75%). Expected value = 6000×0.25 = 1500. Variance = (6000−1500)²×0.25 + (0−1500)²×0.75 = (4500)²×0.25 + (1500)²×0.75 = 5,062,500 + 1,687,500 = 6,750,000. Thus, Lottery B has a higher variance (6,750,000 > 2,750,000), so the reason would prefer Lottery B. The reason is applicable to the decision problem.",
